{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1013251-what-s-your-story-s-level-of-play","id":1013251,"title":"What's Your Story's Level of Play?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-06T10:11:43-08:00","id":1013251,"title":"What's Your Story's Level of Play?","content":"Pretty simple question. As a ST or Player what's your preferred level of play as far as Arete and Spheres.<br /> <br /> As a ST I don't allow my players to begin with more than rank 2 in a sphere but encourage an Arete of 3. The current story has the players all at a Arete of 4 and 1 player has a single sphere (Forces) at 4, Prime at 3 and 2 or 3 others at 2. Another player has 2 in everything except Entropy which is at 3. The other 2 players are simmilar but nothing else is at 4.<br /> <br /> Now I'm about to let them obtain an Arete of 5 (I control Arete gain at 0 xp). How far do you tend to go in your stories? Arete 6+? Is that level of play feasible, or does it tends to get out of control?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T10:49:23-08:00","id":1013268,"title":"","content":"I think that, yes, normal games should go for a max Arete of 5, analog to the other gamelines going to 5 for their player characters at a 'sane' level.<br /> It keeps things 'moderate' to 'mages with quite an oomph', without going into the higher levels of power.<br /> <br /> That said, if you want to do a 'High End Game' type of campaign where the sky's the limit, and the stakes become global and interdimensional that works too, and you can let your mages progress to the high end of Arete over lots and lots and lots of campaigns and sessions.<br /> <br /> You just need to know what your players want, what you as an ST want, and have the required creativity to keep things still challenging for your players in the Endgame. That's pretty much the important part. You mustn't get overwhelmed. Make plans <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T16:49:19-08:00","id":1013481,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd say anything over 5 Arete is just showboating at that point. Once you get to 5 Personal Arete, the sky is the limit on what you can do via Talismans/Devices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T19:13:26-08:00","id":1013533,"title":"","content":"I leave starting Sphere levels RAW (I learned my lesson when I had a game where they started with either 4 or5 dots of Spheres instead of 7. Very sad players). However I start Arete off at 2. But the 3rd dot costs 7 bonus points, like a Sphere, rather than just 4. Bonus point costs should correlate with Experience costs, otherwise it creates a strong incentive for raising certain things at character creation. In RAW, there is an undeniable incentive for spending 8 bonus points to raise Arete from 1 to 3. Which is dumb. Arete of 1 is dumb no matter how many bonus points it costs to raise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T19:23:22-08:00","id":1013539,"title":"","content":"I guess it depends on the group. For most of the games I've been in for the past 20+ years of Mage, Arete up to 10 was &quot;allowable&quot; (though the latter was very, very rare, of course). It's easy to confuse/conflate the Arete rating, in-and-of-itself, as the singular pinnacle of how to look at Mage(tm). We had plenty of mages who never went above Arete:3/4, but had 25-30 dots spread among their spheres (representing the relative &quot;omni-magic&quot; of TV/Movie spellcasting, wherein as long as you had the right spells/rotes/paradigm, you could do a whole lot of everything but not very powerfully &quot;Merlin-on-the-spot&quot;, as it were); conversely, there were several characters who had Arete:7-9, but no sphere above 3 -- their focus was on Enlightenment(tm), proper, and not on &quot;casting spells&quot;, as it were. (Those latter mages were very good, of course, at manifesting relatively powerful -- powerful within the context of mortal men -- workings with little more than a twitch of the nose or very casual gesture; however, that was rarely, if ever, their &quot;thing&quot;.) We also had several Archmages, but again that was played more along the lines of story-driven aspects than &quot;who's got the dots?&quot; -- that pwrgmr schtick that can creep into too many games, but never an issue for our group(s). (A few semi-regular guest players were surprised to find that many of our mages either weren't half as powerful as they (the guests) thought, or were exceptionally more so, simply because we weren't about dots/dice, generally speaking.) And, of course, most of us moved onto using the DA:M system once it came out because it allowed more tailorable metaphysics as well as dice/level settings, and consequently dice pools -- when they came up -- were usually a bit higher than the standard for Ascension. Balancing that, though, were the generally higher (and sometimes *much* higher) Difficulty #s for more complex workings, which consequently kept the use of rituals, mystic times, tass and similar-such more in line with conventional &quot;TV/Movie&quot; magic and spells while still allowing for casual-but-powerful workings for more strongly in-paradigm magic (those spells/effects that required only one Pillar but would have required several Spheres in Ascension to simulate).<br /> <br /> So it really just depends on the people you're playing with and the scaling relative to the depth of narrative vs. &quot;dungeon-crawl&quot; (that is, more dice-mechanic oriented vs. &quot;the game&quot; being secondary to the depth of story involved). Even a mage who happens to have an Arete of 6+ and many dots in various Spheres isn't a game-stopper, by any means. It only becomes an issue, primarily, if pwrgmrz are on the scene and/or &quot;everything is handled by magic(k)&quot; -- one of the lessons learned in advancing Arete to greater depths is that Magic(k)(tm) isn't always the answer to everything, especially in a modern setting where Paradox can get out of hand very quickly if things really go from push-to-shove. Many Masters and Archmages (even those smacking of hubris, from time to time) will stress to their lessers the value of a casual hand in things....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}